{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at e86d9bd. F1 changes the canonical store and reorders an explicit prerequisite; F4 changes the signed definition and stale-intent semantics; F7 replaces S0's Inlay gate. These are legitimate proposals, but section 5's claim that none weakens a gate and F2's claim to be the only accepted-contract change are inaccurate. Please distinguish retaining a later PDS test from retaining the current canonical-PDS contract, and list these as decisions that need adoption. F2's claim that replay ceases to depend on state size is too strong: effect validation can be O(change), while reads, queries, indexes and serialization can still depend on state. Label that benefit narrowly. F6 should qualify its package-version assumption: jsonata 2.2.2 has built-in stack/sequence/timeout options as well as entry/exit hooks; an operation counter still needs a wrapper. These edits concern accuracy of the review note, not rejection of its recommendations. Current implementation remains governed by adopted #28 until a replacement decision is adopted.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:0e4e6450c2ad57007f9221b889bb6a43bf96ef2b","head":"e86d9bd30ccf19f982a06c912e8d10656fd33ee5","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:46cf825a8626a96de7b2068c0b25c997d069b613\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:46cf825a8626a96de7b2068c0b25c997d069b613","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}